WEBVTT

01:55.665 --> 01:59.974
[terrified chatter]

02:00.007 --> 02:02.077
[screaming]

02:02.110 --> 02:02.846
Everybody run!

02:02.879 --> 02:04.448
Hurry! Take cover!

02:17.074 --> 02:18.911
Aide: That was Poltos!

02:20.915 --> 02:22.417
[alarmed grunts]

02:23.688 --> 02:25.558
Fobster: Forgive my intrusion,
but there's no time to waste.

02:26.092 --> 02:27.228
My liege;

02:27.261 --> 02:28.598
News from Carl Kingdom.

02:28.631 --> 02:30.768
It was Queen Flora
who sent me here.

02:34.710 --> 02:37.281
Deroline: [shivering]

02:37.314 --> 02:40.020
Couldn't... you pick
somewhere warmer to hide?!

02:40.054 --> 02:41.489
It's safe out here!

02:41.524 --> 02:43.227
This is the only
place that's safe...

02:43.260 --> 02:44.796
Away from the Dark Army.

02:44.829 --> 02:46.032
I'm starving...

02:46.065 --> 02:47.669
Heroh Heroh: Hey!

02:47.702 --> 02:50.473
You hungry? We caught
us some dinner.

02:55.183 --> 02:57.254
Zulbon: What is that?!

02:57.287 --> 02:59.458
Uh... a bird?

03:01.162 --> 03:04.101
[terrified screaming]

03:04.134 --> 03:06.272
All: Run for it!

03:10.080 --> 03:12.417
[screaming]

03:12.451 --> 03:15.825
Where's the real Hero -
when you need him most?!

03:15.858 --> 03:17.762
[screaming]

03:19.966 --> 03:23.139
Zaboera: [delighted cackle]

03:23.173 --> 03:26.046
What incredible
destructive ability.

03:26.079 --> 03:28.984
King Vearn is great indeed.

03:30.020 --> 03:32.391
Ah, if it isn't my master,

03:32.425 --> 03:35.865
the great spectral
Commander Mystvearn.

03:35.898 --> 03:39.506
Did you see the size
of that crater out there?

03:39.540 --> 03:42.579
I must admit, even
I am still amazed at

03:42.613 --> 03:45.885
the extent of our
king's vast power...

03:45.918 --> 03:49.058
Oh, did I mention that
he also promoted me to be

03:49.091 --> 03:51.563
the Dark Army's
Second-in-Command?

03:51.597 --> 03:54.068
I'm so glad I
had the foresight to

03:54.101 --> 03:56.973
cut ties with
that fool Hadlar.

03:57.943 --> 03:59.178
Mystvearn: Zaboera.

03:59.211 --> 04:00.481
Y-yes?

04:00.515 --> 04:02.251
Mystvearn: During
Hadlar's transformation

04:02.284 --> 04:04.155
into the Superior Being,

04:04.188 --> 04:05.758
did you not notice
the Black Core

04:05.792 --> 04:07.929
that had been
planted inside him?

04:09.165 --> 04:11.703
Well, of course I
noticed. Who wouldn't?

04:11.737 --> 04:14.374
I just thought it was
best to leave it alone.

04:14.408 --> 04:17.882
I knew that King Vearn
would set if off eventually,

04:17.915 --> 04:20.588
but so long as I wasn't
caught in the blast,

04:20.622 --> 04:23.293
it could work
to my advantage.

04:23.326 --> 04:25.564
[devious giggle]

04:28.937 --> 04:30.306
Something wrong?

04:30.942 --> 04:32.310
Mystvearn: You're scum.

04:32.344 --> 04:35.851
Speaking ill of Hadlar
is beyond your station!

04:37.855 --> 04:41.563
Mystvearn: I recognize
your part in saving King Vearn,

04:41.597 --> 04:44.769
but I have no trust
in some gutter rat

04:44.802 --> 04:48.076
with eyes only for
his own success.

04:48.109 --> 04:50.413
Your type always
turn on their masters

04:50.447 --> 04:53.720
when it suits their needs.

04:53.754 --> 04:57.528
Mystvearn: And when you do...
I will not hesitate.

05:02.572 --> 05:04.610
You can threaten
me all you wish.

05:04.643 --> 05:07.815
Dominance is not a
matter of power alone;

05:07.849 --> 05:09.620
one must have
patience and cunning

05:09.653 --> 05:11.756
to be the last one standing.

05:13.293 --> 05:16.299
And I happen to have
those qualities in spades,

05:16.332 --> 05:18.971
so it will be me who
gets the last laugh.

05:37.208 --> 05:39.646
Popp [thought]:
I... I made it.

05:39.680 --> 05:41.816
But how did I end up here?

05:45.490 --> 05:47.194
Popp [thought]:
You swam all this way

05:47.227 --> 05:49.498
carrying me, didn't you?

05:49.532 --> 05:52.104
You never cease to amaze, Maam.

05:52.137 --> 05:54.241
Ursa Major: [growling]

05:54.274 --> 05:55.744
[alarmed grunt]

05:59.352 --> 06:01.188
[growling]

06:01.222 --> 06:03.694
Popp [thought]:
An Ursa Major?!

06:03.727 --> 06:06.432
Without my Magic Power,
I'm no match.

06:07.669 --> 06:10.574
But I have to protect
her at all costs!

06:13.914 --> 06:15.685
Hey, come and get it!

06:15.718 --> 06:18.523
I'll turn you into
a rug - you hear me?!

06:20.427 --> 06:22.464
[threatening snarl]

06:26.606 --> 06:27.775
Popp [thought]:
What's it doing?!

06:27.808 --> 06:30.581
Chiu: Ha! Good job,
Trooper Number Eight!

06:31.650 --> 06:33.319
Greetings, Sir Popp.

06:33.352 --> 06:34.990
And Miss Maam!

06:35.023 --> 06:36.125
[relieved sigh]

06:36.158 --> 06:37.227
You idiots!

06:37.260 --> 06:39.599
Almost gave me a heart-attack.

06:39.633 --> 06:40.902
Akhim: Hang in there, sir.

06:40.935 --> 06:43.105
We'll take you back
to the Forest Fort!

06:43.774 --> 06:45.511
Good job, pal.

06:46.279 --> 06:48.817
The Forest Fort, huh?

06:48.851 --> 06:51.155
Nova: It's the basecamp
for the Order of Carl.

06:51.189 --> 06:52.324
They're back in the fight.

06:52.357 --> 06:54.630
Queen Flora and some
of her forces survived.

06:54.663 --> 06:56.332
Some kinda miracle, huh?

06:56.365 --> 06:57.902
[relieved sigh]

06:59.940 --> 07:02.477
Popp: So, it's been
four whole days?

07:02.512 --> 07:03.981
Leona: And in that time...

07:04.015 --> 07:06.119
The Dark Army has been
using their flying fortress

07:06.152 --> 07:09.425
to bombard towns and
cities all over the world.

07:09.458 --> 07:11.462
One target every day.

07:11.496 --> 07:13.534
You know, I did
think it was odd

07:13.567 --> 07:15.805
that they weren't
attacking the capitals,

07:15.838 --> 07:18.678
but if their goal is sheer
destruction, it makes sense.

07:18.711 --> 07:20.179
It doesn't matter now.

07:20.213 --> 07:23.486
If King Vearn wants to
wipe out the Surface World,

07:23.521 --> 07:27.127
I'd rather have to deal
with an invasion, honestly.

07:28.897 --> 07:31.936
But at least the two of you
made it back in one piece!

07:31.970 --> 07:35.476
And I'm sure Dai and the
others will be here soon...

07:35.511 --> 07:38.316
I sure hope you're right.

07:38.349 --> 07:40.654
Things weren't
looking so good...

07:40.688 --> 07:44.261
I mean, the Holy Mother Dragon
flew in and took Dai away.

07:44.295 --> 07:47.434
And then Hyunckel and
Crocodine took a direct hit

07:47.467 --> 07:49.472
from the Dark King's magic.

07:49.506 --> 07:51.543
If Hadlar hadn't
shown up when he did,

07:51.576 --> 07:53.747
it would have been
the end of us.

07:54.549 --> 07:58.824
We got our butts
kicked. Seriously.

07:58.857 --> 08:00.695
Leona [thought]: It's no use.

08:00.728 --> 08:02.097
Popp and Maam have both felt

08:02.130 --> 08:06.138
the terrifying force of
the Dark King - firsthand.

08:06.171 --> 08:09.078
There... there isn't
anything we could say

08:09.111 --> 08:10.714
to lift their spirits.

08:11.281 --> 08:12.718
Popp: I guess...

08:12.752 --> 08:16.125
There's just nothing at all we
can do to stop them, is there?

08:17.060 --> 08:20.066
Flora: You mustn't
say such gloomy things.

08:20.100 --> 08:21.101
[surprised breaths]

08:24.475 --> 08:25.912
Flora: After all...

08:25.945 --> 08:28.917
You are Avan's
disciples. Aren't you?

08:29.953 --> 08:30.955
Huh?

08:30.988 --> 08:32.391
Ah, Queen Flora!

08:32.424 --> 08:34.261
Oh! The leader of Carl!

08:34.294 --> 08:35.296
That's right.

08:35.330 --> 08:37.067
She escaped the
fall of her kingdom

08:37.101 --> 08:38.704
with a handful of knights.

08:38.737 --> 08:40.508
They want to join
forces with us

08:40.541 --> 08:42.310
and strike back
at the Dark Army.

08:44.381 --> 08:48.156
Leona: We've all been holed up
here planning our next move.

08:48.189 --> 08:50.460
Now, Popp... Maam.

08:50.494 --> 08:52.364
I know you're distraught.

08:52.397 --> 08:54.267
But you must take heart.

08:54.301 --> 08:57.441
If you really wish to carry
on the will of Sir Avan,

08:57.474 --> 09:00.279
then you cannot give
in to such weakness.

09:01.616 --> 09:03.987
Popp: Whoa, you
knew Master Avan?

09:04.021 --> 09:07.294
As a matter of fact, he
once belonged to our Order.

09:07.328 --> 09:08.731
Avan fought bravely

09:08.764 --> 09:13.640
to defend our kingdom along
with my lead knight, Sir Roka.

09:15.578 --> 09:19.017
Yes, Maam. I knew
your father, as well.

09:24.128 --> 09:25.330
Back then...

09:25.363 --> 09:30.473
Lord Hadlar led the Dark Army,
laying siege to our domain.

09:30.508 --> 09:33.112
My father had grown ill...

09:33.146 --> 09:34.347
So the throne fell to me.

09:34.381 --> 09:38.322
I led our kingdom's fight
against the growing darkness.

09:38.657 --> 09:40.026
[cheering]

09:40.060 --> 09:42.698
Flora: I tried my best
to put on a brave face

09:42.732 --> 09:45.538
and boost the morale
of my subjects,

09:45.571 --> 09:47.609
but I wasn't sure we
could actually overcome

09:47.642 --> 09:50.948
the supernatural powers
of the Dark Lord.

09:50.982 --> 09:54.790
But really...
I was terrified.

09:54.823 --> 09:56.458
And it wasn't just me.

09:56.491 --> 09:58.531
Everyone in the
palace was afraid.

09:58.564 --> 09:59.732
Knight: It's useless.

09:59.766 --> 10:02.304
There's no way we can
outmatch the Dark Lord!

10:02.337 --> 10:05.143
Minister: If we just keep
scampering around like this,

10:05.177 --> 10:06.913
we'll gain nothing.

10:06.947 --> 10:09.184
Flora: But Avan
refused to give up.

10:09.217 --> 10:10.721
Avan: No, no, no.

10:10.755 --> 10:13.158
It's time to pull
yourselves together, men!

10:13.192 --> 10:17.034
If we do nothing, then we
really will gain nothing here.

10:17.067 --> 10:21.075
The way I see it, if all we
can do is "scamper" around...

10:21.108 --> 10:22.243
Then my friends...

10:22.277 --> 10:24.014
"Scamper", we shall!

10:32.331 --> 10:44.388
[laughing]

10:44.421 --> 10:45.824
Flora: I just
couldn't help it.

10:45.858 --> 10:50.433
I burst out laughing. Right
there in front of everyone.

10:50.467 --> 10:51.937
That's when I realized...

10:51.970 --> 10:57.915
this man is a natural-born
Hero. He can inspire anyone.

10:59.118 --> 11:03.794
And so nowadays, whenever I
feel like I've lost hope...

11:03.827 --> 11:06.900
I remember I can still
"scamper around."

11:06.933 --> 11:08.570
And I hear his voice...

11:08.604 --> 11:10.707
Telling me not to give up.

11:13.479 --> 11:16.184
Popp: Um... Your Majesty...

11:19.592 --> 11:21.095
Master Avan...

11:21.128 --> 11:24.234
It's all right, Popp.
I know he's gone.

11:25.269 --> 11:27.575
Flora: If he were still
out there somewhere,

11:27.608 --> 11:30.514
he would never have
let things go this far.

11:30.548 --> 11:32.183
The destruction
of his own home.

11:32.216 --> 11:36.391
I'm certain, that if he were
able, he'd be by my side.

11:37.728 --> 11:40.901
Popp [thought]: Oh.
I get it. So, she...

11:40.935 --> 11:45.944
Maam [thought]: She was in love
with Master Avan, wasn't she?

11:56.566 --> 11:58.235
"Scamper," huh?

11:58.269 --> 12:00.541
Sounds like a plan.

12:00.574 --> 12:02.077
Yeah, count me in.

12:02.110 --> 12:03.045
[chuckling]

12:03.078 --> 12:05.984
I may never be quite
as brave Master Avan,

12:06.018 --> 12:09.157
but I know I can scamper
with the best of 'em!

12:11.261 --> 12:12.464
Many thanks...

12:12.497 --> 12:15.469
But for now you must rest
- the time will come.

12:17.808 --> 12:19.645
Get yourselves in
fighting shape.

12:19.679 --> 12:23.520
I have a plan of
my own. You'll see.

12:26.593 --> 12:27.895
She's a great woman.

12:27.929 --> 12:29.933
It's almost as if
her mere presence...

12:29.966 --> 12:32.070
leaves a charge in the air.

12:32.103 --> 12:33.272
No kidding.

12:33.306 --> 12:36.847
I can definitely see why you
respect her so much, Leona.

12:36.880 --> 12:40.019
Popp: So she and
Master Avan were a thing.

12:40.053 --> 12:43.159
I mean, she does have
that mature appeal...

12:43.192 --> 12:45.196
[giggle]

12:45.229 --> 12:46.465
Both: Scumbag!

12:46.498 --> 12:47.301
[pained groan]

12:47.334 --> 12:48.436
Bowson: Princess Leona!

12:48.469 --> 12:49.639
Your presence is needed.

12:49.672 --> 12:52.477
The Dark Army is moving
against Ringaia!

12:52.511 --> 12:53.546
[worried breaths]

13:12.551 --> 13:16.459
Vearn: I forgot how boring it
can be when all our affairs

13:16.492 --> 13:18.129
are running smoothly.

13:18.162 --> 13:20.132
Zaboera: I wholeheartedly agree.

13:20.166 --> 13:22.871
Killvearn: I wouldn't
be so sure.

13:26.880 --> 13:29.418
This card represents
misfortune...

13:29.451 --> 13:32.624
And it comes up no matter
how many times I shuffle.

13:32.658 --> 13:34.294
Perhaps it foretells
of yet another

13:34.327 --> 13:37.367
resistance looming
upon our horizon.

13:37.400 --> 13:38.435
Killvearn: Perhaps...

13:38.469 --> 13:42.110
But whatever it means,
it's definitely trouble.

13:42.144 --> 13:45.784
My cards have never been
wrong before, Your Majesty.

13:45.818 --> 13:48.088
Then let us draw them out.

13:48.122 --> 13:52.363
We can make some use of those
two we've been holding captive.

13:53.600 --> 13:56.873
Canal: Your Majesty!
Outside! Look in the sky!

13:58.075 --> 13:59.980
King Teran:
The Holy Mother Dragon.

14:00.013 --> 14:01.281
This can only mean that

14:01.315 --> 14:05.123
the life of a Dragon Knight
is coming to an end...

14:05.156 --> 14:07.127
and the God of
Dragons has chosen

14:07.160 --> 14:09.599
our people to be witnesses.

14:09.632 --> 14:11.201
Canal: Could it be the Hero?!

14:34.949 --> 14:36.384
Dai: Where am I?

14:38.155 --> 14:41.863
What... What happened to me?

14:41.897 --> 14:42.865
Holy Dragon: Death.

14:42.898 --> 14:43.900
[startled breath]

14:43.934 --> 14:45.336
Holy Dragon:
The end of your path.

14:47.508 --> 14:48.777
And who are you?

14:48.810 --> 14:51.449
Holy Dragon: I am
the Holy Mother Dragon,

14:51.482 --> 14:53.018
a servant of the gods.

14:53.051 --> 14:56.893
I preside over the eternal
cycle of the Dragon Knights.

14:56.926 --> 14:58.496
The Mother Dragon?

14:58.530 --> 15:00.299
That's right...

15:00.333 --> 15:03.406
You're the being who passes
on the Crest's power...

15:03.439 --> 15:06.813
from one Dragon Knight
to whichever one is next.

15:06.846 --> 15:09.685
I still kinda feel
like I'm alive, though.

15:09.718 --> 15:11.221
Holy Dragon:
Allow me to explain.

15:11.255 --> 15:15.363
You have taken on an astral
form and are between realms.

15:15.396 --> 15:20.206
Soon your spirit shall pass
on into the world of the gods.

15:20.240 --> 15:23.914
I see. So will another...

15:23.947 --> 15:25.751
Dragon Knight replace me, or...

15:25.784 --> 15:30.493
Holy Dragon: No. There will
be no more Dragon Knights.

15:31.796 --> 15:34.101
Holy Dragon: You
are the last, Dai.

15:34.134 --> 15:37.039
Wait! But... But, why?!

15:37.073 --> 15:38.610
Holy Dragon:
The gods who designed

15:38.643 --> 15:40.246
the realm you call home

15:40.280 --> 15:42.383
created the Dragon
Knights in order to

15:42.417 --> 15:45.189
prevent the forces
of evil from tipping

15:45.223 --> 15:47.493
the natural
balance of the world.

15:48.362 --> 15:51.001
But it seems that
over many eons,

15:51.035 --> 15:54.509
the power of such evil
has managed to evolve.

15:54.542 --> 15:57.515
Now the Dark King Vearn
possesses a power

15:57.548 --> 16:02.424
that could rival the
very gods themselves.

16:02.457 --> 16:05.196
Holy Dragon: Even with
the might of a Dragon Knight,

16:05.229 --> 16:07.568
evil can no longer be thwarted.

16:07.601 --> 16:10.674
In fact, the desire
to overcome your kind

16:10.707 --> 16:15.383
may be what drove evil to
evolve in the first place.

16:15.416 --> 16:16.819
Do you understand?

16:16.852 --> 16:18.121
B-But... I...

16:18.155 --> 16:20.727
Holy Dragon: That is why
I must bring the history of

16:20.760 --> 16:23.567
the Dragon Knights to an end.

16:23.600 --> 16:27.508
I no longer have the power to
create a new Knight, anyway.

16:27.541 --> 16:31.583
The growing darkness
has covered the world,

16:31.616 --> 16:35.256
weakening me as well.

16:35.290 --> 16:40.567
You mean... you're really just
going to let the Dark King win?

16:44.508 --> 16:46.613
Holy Dragon: The trials
of the mortal world

16:46.646 --> 16:48.684
no longer concern you.

16:48.717 --> 16:54.360
Let them go, and I shall return
your spirit to the heavens.

17:00.841 --> 17:02.343
Holy Dragon:
Something is wrong...

17:02.376 --> 17:05.215
You have two souls within you.

17:15.905 --> 17:17.574
Dai: Dad?!

17:17.608 --> 17:19.579
Holy Mother Dragon,

17:19.612 --> 17:22.451
the boy is not your
last true Knight...

17:22.484 --> 17:23.520
I am.

17:23.553 --> 17:27.394
Dai is my son, and his
mother Soala was a human.

17:27.427 --> 17:30.901
If you must take a soul,
then take mine.

17:30.934 --> 17:33.439
Holy Dragon: A child?!
That cannot be.

17:33.473 --> 17:36.646
He still has many
years ahead of him.

17:36.680 --> 17:38.181
So please, I beseech you.

17:38.215 --> 17:40.821
Will you grant
him another chance?

17:40.854 --> 17:42.223
Whoa, wait...

17:42.257 --> 17:44.327
Holy Dragon: Even if
I do revive him,

17:44.361 --> 17:47.467
he will only face
another cruel loss.

17:47.500 --> 17:49.572
No one can defeat
the Dark King,

17:49.605 --> 17:52.276
no matter what power
they might possess.

17:52.309 --> 17:54.849
I do not think
that is the case.

17:54.882 --> 17:56.452
My son has a strength

17:56.485 --> 17:59.258
no ordinary Dragon
Knight possesses.

17:59.291 --> 18:01.829
Something beyond power.

18:01.863 --> 18:03.298
Holy Dragon: But...

18:03.332 --> 18:07.473
If every generation is meant to
receive only one Dragon Knight,

18:07.508 --> 18:11.515
then tell me - how was
I able to sire a child?

18:11.549 --> 18:14.354
So now, I believe that
the gods have realized

18:14.388 --> 18:18.195
our limitations and decided
to give us a new hope.

18:18.228 --> 18:22.236
Power may rule over everything
in this world, but...

18:22.270 --> 18:25.109
hope is the
greatest power of all.

18:25.143 --> 18:27.280
And perhaps that is
the reason why

18:27.313 --> 18:29.818
this boy was
allowed to be born.

18:31.789 --> 18:34.695
Please, Mother. Revive him.

18:38.837 --> 18:39.772
Holy Dragon: Very well.

18:39.805 --> 18:42.878
I shall grant Dai what
remains of my power,

18:42.911 --> 18:46.217
giving him one, final chance.

18:49.257 --> 18:51.161
Baran: Dai...

18:51.194 --> 18:52.564
From here on out,

18:52.598 --> 18:56.171
the history of the Dragon
Knights will be yours to write.

18:56.204 --> 18:58.843
One day you may
even be a father.

18:58.876 --> 19:02.851
But first of all, you
must defeat King Vearn...

19:02.885 --> 19:04.889
And I know you will.

19:04.922 --> 19:06.358
But I just can't.

19:06.391 --> 19:10.934
I'm not... I'm nowhere
near as strong as you are!

19:10.968 --> 19:13.941
I'll never beat
the Dark King alone!

19:13.974 --> 19:16.145
You are not alone, son.

19:16.178 --> 19:18.048
You have your friends.

19:18.081 --> 19:19.786
Dai: No, Dad-

19:19.819 --> 19:21.355
Baran: Your mother and I...

19:21.388 --> 19:23.927
will be by your side, as well.

19:23.960 --> 19:26.632
No, wait - please, don't go.

19:27.567 --> 19:30.507
Please, Dad...

19:50.581 --> 19:55.255
Please, Dad...
please don't go.

19:56.626 --> 19:57.962
Quickly now.

19:57.995 --> 19:59.598
Fetch a Mage at once!

19:59.632 --> 20:02.003
We must get him
to Queen Flora!

20:02.036 --> 20:02.938
Canal: Yes, sire!

20:14.194 --> 20:16.932
Maybe we should give
them some space?

20:24.147 --> 20:25.550
Oh, Dai.

20:25.584 --> 20:28.990
I'm so glad...
you'll be all right.

20:33.365 --> 20:35.002
Popp: Queen Flora.

20:35.036 --> 20:36.673
Dai has been fully healed.

20:36.706 --> 20:39.411
He's resting now,
but he'll pull through.

20:39.444 --> 20:42.484
I see. Well, that's a relief.

20:42.518 --> 20:44.655
Very good news indeed.

20:44.688 --> 20:49.297
Only... I'm afraid I've received
some bad news, as well.

20:49.330 --> 20:51.535
The Dark Army
has sent a message

20:51.569 --> 20:54.240
to every kingdom
across the world...

20:54.273 --> 20:57.046
etched in old runes
appearing on mirrors.

20:57.080 --> 21:00.587
When translated,
here's what it says:

21:00.620 --> 21:03.726
"To the doomed leaders
of the humans...

21:03.760 --> 21:06.397
Your end draws near.

21:06.431 --> 21:09.839
In a few days, the forces
of our Dark Army shall rise up

21:09.872 --> 21:14.380
and wipe your pathetic
Surface World from existence.

21:14.414 --> 21:18.523
There is nothing you
can do to stop us,

21:18.556 --> 21:23.365
so make peace with your fate
and accept the inevitable.

21:23.399 --> 21:26.071
To commemorate this
grand achievement,

21:26.104 --> 21:28.042
we shall make an
example of the traitors

21:28.075 --> 21:30.012
who aided your fallen Hero:

21:30.046 --> 21:36.258
Hyunckel the Dark Swordsman and
the mighty Beast King Crocodine.

21:36.291 --> 21:38.329
We welcome all
who are interested

21:38.362 --> 21:40.900
to witness this punishment.

21:40.934 --> 21:42.672
Two days from now at noon,

21:42.705 --> 21:45.476
in the northern mountains
of Carl Kingdom,

21:45.510 --> 21:48.415
they will both perish."

21:48.448 --> 21:50.520
Those no-good,
spineless cowards.

21:50.554 --> 21:52.423
There must be
something we can do.

21:52.457 --> 21:54.828
We can't let them
go through with it.

21:55.697 --> 21:58.034
We must have a
meeting at once!

23:37.667 --> 23:39.337
Narrator: With
Hyunckel and Crocodine

23:39.370 --> 23:41.074
held captive
by the Dark Army,

23:41.107 --> 23:43.846
Dai awakes fully recovered
after his encounter with

23:43.880 --> 23:46.519
Baran and the
Holy Mother Dragon.

23:46.552 --> 23:49.023
And although his wounds
have been healed,

23:49.057 --> 23:53.064
the memory of his last defeat
continues to torment him.

23:53.098 --> 23:55.603
The others believe Dai
will regain his stride,

23:55.637 --> 23:58.510
but will it be in time
to save their friends?

23:58.543 --> 23:59.979
Find out next time on

24:00.012 --> 24:02.483
Dragon Quest:
The Adventure of Dai,

24:02.517 --> 24:04.220
"Dai and Popp".
